    "title": "Metro Diner Has Been Open Every Hour Since 1964; Nobody's Touched a Thing - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Steven Doyle ,\n4 hours ago It’s 3:40 in the morning on West Davis Street, and the lights are on at Metro Diner the way they’ve been on every night since Lyndon Johnson was in the White House. A cook flips something on the flattop. A waitress tops off a mug for a guy in scrubs who just got off a shift at Methodist. Nobody looks up when the door opens. In Oak Cliff, that’s just Tuesday. Read full article",
